<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arcesilaus III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 515 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Arcesilaus III of Cyrene</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arcesilaus III was a Battiad king of Cyrene in the later 6th century BCE, son of Battus III and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pheretime">Pheretime</a>. He tried to restore the royal powers curbed by the reforms of Demonax, was driven into exile, returned with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a> and submitted to the Persian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambyses-ii">Cambyses II</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> records that he was murdered at Barca, which led his mother to call in a Persian army.</p></div>
